  "title": "Gameplay Atlas: Develop & interact",
  "date": "2026-11-24T22:00:00.000Z",
  "content": "Gameplay Atlas: Develop & interact\n\nThese genres basically focus on storytelling. I used to make an interactive novel - 1944. I really wish I had read this part before making it.\n\nTopics\n\nThe themes here are progression, relationships, cooperation, and dialogue.\n\nProgression & legacy\n\nExclusive specialization branches (different skill branches)\n\nPractice-based skill growth\n\nRefund and reassign upgrades\n\nPersistent currency between attempts (roguelike)\n\nChoose the next heir (roguelike)\n\nReset progress for lasting acceleration\n\nEscalating challenge conditions (harder levels)\n\nRandom choices at level-up\n\nComplete a weapon evolution recipe\n\nResearch prerequisite chains (skill → weapon upgrades)\n\nDeath costs trained abilities\n\nProgress through learned knowledge\n\nThe examples are:\n\nGrim Dawn\nGrim Dawn\n\nThe Elder Scrolls V: Skyrim Special Edition\nThe Elder Scrolls V: Skyrim Special Edition\n\nBaldur's Gate 3\nBaldur's Gate 3\n\nHades\nHades\n\nRogue Legacy 2\nRogue Legacy 2\n\nRogue Legacy\nRogue Legacy\n\nCookie Clicker\nCookie Clicker\n\nClicker Heroes\nClicker Heroes\n\nSlay the Spire\nSlay the Spire\n\nVampire Survivors\nVampire Survivors\n\nBrotato\nBrotato\n\nHoloCure - Save the Fans!\nHoloCure - Save the Fans!\n\nFactorio\nFactorio\n\nRimWorld\nRimWorld\n\nOuter Wilds\nOuter Wilds\n\nTUNIC\nTUNIC\n\nSocial & relationships\n\nGift preferences and allocation\n\nDaily contact rhythm\n\nRelationship-gated scenes\n\nCompanion approval\n\nDialogue persuasion checks\n\nShared-activity itineraries\n\nFaction reputation (two parties record the player's reputation)\n\nSecrets as leverage\n\nRelationship commitment (upgrading the relationship)\n\nThe examples are:\n\nMy Time at Portia\nMy Time at Portia\n\nPersona 4 Golden\nPersona 4 Golden\n\nDisco Elysium\nDisco Elysium\n\nTyranny\nTyranny\n\nFallout: New Vegas\nFallout: New Vegas\n\nCrusader Kings III (dynastic marriage)\nCrusader Kings III\n\nBeholder\nBeholder\n\nTotal War: THREE KINGDOMS\nTotal War: THREE KINGDOMS\n\nCooperation & social play\n\nCommunicating split information (one piece of information split among different people)\n\nHidden roles and convincing behavior\n\nDiscussion, evidence and voting\n\nReviving a downed teammate\n\nCrewing a shared vehicle\n\nMoving while physically tethered\n\nReaching separate controls and synchronizing\n\nCombining different character abilities\n\nTemporary alliances and betrayal\n\nThe examples are:\n\nKeep Talking and Nobody Explodes\nKeep Talking and Nobody Explodes\n\nWe Were Here\nWe Were Here\n\nAmong Us\nAmong Us\n\nGoose Goose Duck\nGoose Goose Duck\n\nDeep Rock Galactic\nDeep Rock Galactic\n\nSea of Thieves\nSea of Thieves\n\nLovers in a Dangerous Spacetime\nLovers in a Dangerous Spacetime\n\nBread & Fred\nBread & Fred\n\nChained Together\nChained Together\n\nPortal 2\nPortal 2\n\nTrine 2\nTrine 2\n\nArmello\nArmello\n\nJourney of Greed\nJourney of Greed\n\nDialogue & event choices\n\nAnswer before the response window closes\n\nChoose silence and let the other person continue\n\nUse evidence to challenge a specific statement\n\nLet an earlier choice change a later event\n\nAllocate limited time among leads (separate work with one timeline)\n\nOpen extra dialogue through identity and experience\n\nRespond through what you make and serve\n\nContinue earlier consequences through another character\n\nRepeat a time window with a different event plan\n\nIntervene before the other person finishes\n\nThe examples are:\n\nThe Walking Dead: Season Two\nThe Walking Dead: Season Two\n\nOxenfree\nOxenfree\n\nPhoenix Wright: Ace Attorney Trilogy\nPhoenix Wright: Ace Attorney Trilogy\n\nPentiment\nPentiment\n\nDisco Elysium\nDisco Elysium\n\nBaldur's Gate 3\nBaldur's Gate 3\n\nVA-11 Hall-A: Cyberpunk Bartender Action\nVA-11 Hall-A: Cyberpunk Bartender Action\n\nCoffee Talk\nCoffee Talk\n\n428: Shibuya Scramble\n428: Shibuya Scramble\n\nDetroit: Become Human\nDetroit: Become Human\n\nTwelve Minutes\nTwelve Minutes\n\nOuter Wilds\nOuter Wilds\n\nMass Effect 2 (2010 Edition)\nMass Effect 2 (2010 Edition)",
